From: TDVP Device Team <devices@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: detect time.h used by core and plugins

HAVE_TIME_H guards declarations in several compilation units, but the
released configure.ac checks sys/time.h only. Detect both headers so
modern compilers receive the standard time and clock declarations.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1230,1 +1230,1 @@
-AC_CHECK_HEADERS_ONCE([sys/time.h])
+AC_CHECK_HEADERS_ONCE([time.h sys/time.h])
